#: ../../library/rp2.rst:4
msgid ":mod:`rp2` --- functionality specific to the RP2040"
msgstr ":mod:`rp2` --- funcionalidad específica del RP2040"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:9
msgid ""
"The ``rp2`` module contains functions and classes specific to the RP2040, as"
" used in the Raspberry Pi Pico."
msgstr ""
"El módulo ``rp2`` contiene funciones y clases específicas del RP2040, tal "
"como se utiliza en la Raspberry Pi Pico."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:12
msgid ""
"See the `RP2040 Python datasheet "
"<https://datasheets.raspberrypi.com/pico/raspberry-pi-pico-python-sdk.pdf>`_"
" for more information, and `pico-micropython-examples "
"<https://github.com/raspberrypi/pico-micropython-examples/tree/master/pio>`_"
" for example code."
msgstr ""
"Consulte la `hoja de datos de Python para el RP2040 "
"<https://datasheets.raspberrypi.com/pico/raspberry-pi-pico-python-sdk.pdf>`_"
" para obtener más información, y `pico-micropython-examples "
"<https://github.com/raspberrypi/pico-micropython-examples/tree/master/pio>`_"
" para ver código de ejemplo."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:20
msgid "PIO related functions"
msgstr "Funciones relacionadas con PIO"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:22
msgid "The ``rp2`` module includes functions for assembling PIO programs."
msgstr "El módulo ``rp2`` incluye funciones para ensamblar programas PIO."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:24
msgid "For running PIO programs, see :class:`rp2.StateMachine`."
msgstr "Para ejecutar programas PIO, consulte :class:`rp2.StateMachine`."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:28
msgid "Assemble a PIO program."
msgstr "Ensambla un programa PIO."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:30
msgid ""
"The following parameters control the initial state of the GPIO pins, as one "
"of `PIO.IN_LOW`, `PIO.IN_HIGH`, `PIO.OUT_LOW` or `PIO.OUT_HIGH`. If the "
"program uses more than one pin, provide a tuple, e.g. "
"``out_init=(PIO.OUT_LOW, PIO.OUT_LOW)``."
msgstr ""
"Los siguientes parámetros controlan el estado inicial de los pines GPIO, "
"como uno de `PIO.IN_LOW`, `PIO.IN_HIGH`, `PIO.OUT_LOW` o `PIO.OUT_HIGH`. Si "
"el programa usa más de un pin, proporcione una tupla, p. ej. "
"``out_init=(PIO.OUT_LOW, PIO.OUT_LOW)``."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:35
msgid "*out_init* configures the pins used for ``out()`` instructions."
msgstr ""
"*out_init* configura los pines usados para las instrucciones ``out()``."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:36
msgid ""
"*set_init* configures the pins used for ``set()`` instructions. There can be"
" at most 5."
msgstr ""
"*set_init* configura los pines usados para las instrucciones ``set()``. "
"Puede haber como máximo 5."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:38
msgid ""
"*sideset_init* configures the pins used for ``.side()`` modifiers. There can"
" be at most 5."
msgstr ""
"*sideset_init* configura los pines usados para los modificadores "
"``.side()``. Puede haber como máximo 5."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:40
msgid ""
"*side_pindir* when set to ``True`` configures ``.side()`` modifiers to be "
"used for pin directions, instead of pin values (the default, when "
"``False``)."
msgstr ""
"*side_pindir*, cuando se establece en ``True``, configura los modificadores "
"``.side()`` para que se usen con las direcciones de los pines, en lugar de "
"con los valores de los pines (el comportamiento predeterminado, cuando es "
"``False``)."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:43
msgid ""
"The following parameters are used by default, but can be overridden in "
"`StateMachine.init()`:"
msgstr ""
"Los siguientes parámetros se usan de forma predeterminada, pero pueden "
"sobrescribirse en `StateMachine.init()`:"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:46
msgid ""
"*in_shiftdir* is the default direction the ISR will shift, either "
"`PIO.SHIFT_LEFT` or `PIO.SHIFT_RIGHT`."
msgstr ""
"*in_shiftdir* es la dirección predeterminada en la que desplazará el ISR, ya"
" sea `PIO.SHIFT_LEFT` o `PIO.SHIFT_RIGHT`."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:48
msgid ""
"*out_shiftdir* is the default direction the OSR will shift, either "
"`PIO.SHIFT_LEFT` or `PIO.SHIFT_RIGHT`."
msgstr ""
"*out_shiftdir* es la dirección predeterminada en la que desplazará el OSR, "
"ya sea `PIO.SHIFT_LEFT` o `PIO.SHIFT_RIGHT`."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:50
msgid ""
"*push_thresh* is the threshold in bits before auto-push or conditional re-"
"pushing is triggered."
msgstr ""
"*push_thresh* es el umbral en bits antes de que se active el auto-push o el "
"re-push condicional."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:52
msgid ""
"*pull_thresh* is the threshold in bits before auto-pull or conditional re-"
"pulling is triggered."
msgstr ""
"*pull_thresh* es el umbral en bits antes de que se active el auto-pull o el "
"re-pull condicional."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:55
msgid "The remaining parameters are:"
msgstr "Los parámetros restantes son:"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:57
msgid "*autopush* configures whether auto-push is enabled."
msgstr "*autopush* configura si el auto-push está habilitado."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:58
msgid "*autopull* configures whether auto-pull is enabled."
msgstr "*autopull* configura si el auto-pull está habilitado."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:59
msgid ""
"*fifo_join* configures whether the 4-word TX and RX FIFOs should be combined"
" into a single 8-word FIFO for one direction only. The options are "
"`PIO.JOIN_NONE`, `PIO.JOIN_RX` and `PIO.JOIN_TX`."
msgstr ""
"*fifo_join* configura si las FIFO de TX y RX de 4 palabras deben combinarse "
"en una sola FIFO de 8 palabras para una única dirección. Las opciones son "
"`PIO.JOIN_NONE`, `PIO.JOIN_RX` y `PIO.JOIN_TX`."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:65
msgid ""
"Assemble a single PIO instruction. You usually want to use `asm_pio()` "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Ensambla una sola instrucción PIO. Normalmente conviene usar `asm_pio()` en "
"su lugar."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:73
msgid ""
"Temporarily turns the QSPI_SS pin into an input and reads its value, "
"returning 1 for low and 0 for high. On a typical RP2040 board with a BOOTSEL"
" button, a return value of 1 indicates that the button is pressed."
msgstr ""
"Convierte temporalmente el pin QSPI_SS en una entrada y lee su valor, "
"devolviendo 1 para nivel bajo y 0 para nivel alto. En una placa RP2040 "
"típica con un botón BOOTSEL, un valor de retorno de 1 indica que el botón "
"está presionado."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:78
msgid ""
"Since this function temporarily disables access to the external flash "
"memory, it also temporarily disables interrupts and the other core to "
"prevent them from trying to execute code from flash."
msgstr ""
"Dado que esta función deshabilita temporalmente el acceso a la memoria flash"
" externa, también deshabilita temporalmente las interrupciones y el otro "
"núcleo para evitar que intenten ejecutar código desde la memoria flash."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:84
msgid ""
"This exception is raised from `asm_pio()` or `asm_pio_encode()` if there is "
"an error assembling a PIO program."
msgstr ""
"Esta excepción se genera desde `asm_pio()` o `asm_pio_encode()` si ocurre un"
" error al ensamblar un programa PIO."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:89
msgid "PIO assembly language instructions"
msgstr "Instrucciones del lenguaje ensamblador PIO"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:91
msgid ""
"PIO state machines are programmed in a custom assembly language with nine "
"core PIO-machine instructions.  In MicroPython, PIO assembly routines are "
"written as a Python function with the decorator ``@rp2.asm_pio()``, and they"
" use Python syntax.  Such routines support standard Python variables and "
"arithmetic, as well as the following custom functions that encode PIO "
"instructions and direct the assembler.  See sec 3.4 of the RP2040 datasheet "
"for further details."
msgstr ""
"Las máquinas de estados PIO se programan en un lenguaje ensamblador "
"personalizado con nueve instrucciones básicas de la máquina PIO. En "
"MicroPython, las rutinas en ensamblador PIO se escriben como una función de "
"Python con el decorador ``@rp2.asm_pio()``, y usan la sintaxis de Python. "
"Dichas rutinas admiten variables y operaciones aritméticas estándar de "
"Python, así como las siguientes funciones personalizadas que codifican las "
"instrucciones PIO y dirigen el ensamblador. Consulte la sección 3.4 de la "
"hoja de datos del RP2040 para obtener más detalles."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:98
msgid "wrap_target()"
msgstr "wrap_target()"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:99
msgid ""
"Specify the location where execution continues after program wrapping. By "
"default this is the start of the PIO routine."
msgstr ""
"Especifica la ubicación donde continúa la ejecución tras el ajuste (wrap) "
"del programa. De forma predeterminada, es el inicio de la rutina PIO."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:102
msgid "wrap()"
msgstr "wrap()"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:103
msgid ""
"Specify the location where the program finishes and wraps around. If this "
"directive is not used then it is added automatically at the end of the PIO "
"routine.  Wrapping does not cost any execution cycles."
msgstr ""
"Especifica la ubicación donde el programa termina y se ajusta (wrap). Si no "
"se usa esta directiva, se añade automáticamente al final de la rutina PIO. "
"El ajuste no consume ningún ciclo de ejecución."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:107
msgid "label(label)"
msgstr "label(label)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:108
msgid ""
"Define a label called *label* at the current location.  *label* can be a "
"string or integer."
msgstr ""
"Define una etiqueta llamada *label* en la ubicación actual. *label* puede "
"ser una cadena o un entero."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:111
msgid "word(instr, label=None)"
msgstr "word(instr, label=None)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:112
msgid "Insert an arbitrary 16-bit word in the assembled output."
msgstr "Inserta una palabra arbitraria de 16 bits en la salida ensamblada."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:114
msgid "*instr*: the 16-bit value"
msgstr "*instr*: el valor de 16 bits"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:115
msgid ""
"*label*: if given, look up the label and logical-or the label's value with "
"*instr*"
msgstr ""
"*label*: si se proporciona, busca la etiqueta y aplica un OR lógico entre el"
" valor de la etiqueta e *instr*"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:118
msgid "jmp(...)"
msgstr "jmp(...)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:119
msgid "This instruction takes two forms:"
msgstr "Esta instrucción admite dos formas:"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:121
msgid "jmp(label)"
msgstr "jmp(label)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:122
msgid "*label*: label to jump to unconditionally"
msgstr "*label*: etiqueta a la que saltar incondicionalmente"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:124
msgid "jmp(cond, label)"
msgstr "jmp(cond, label)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:125
msgid "*cond*: the condition to check, one of:"
msgstr "*cond*: la condición a comprobar, una de:"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:127
msgid "``not_x``, ``not_y``: true if register is zero"
msgstr "``not_x``, ``not_y``: verdadero si el registro es cero"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:128
msgid ""
"``x_dec``, ``y_dec``: true if register is non-zero, and do post decrement"
msgstr ""
"``x_dec``, ``y_dec``: verdadero si el registro es distinto de cero, y "
"realiza un decremento posterior"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:130
msgid "``x_not_y``: true if X is not equal to Y"
msgstr "``x_not_y``: verdadero si X no es igual a Y"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:131
msgid "``pin``: true if the input pin is set"
msgstr "``pin``: verdadero si el pin de entrada está activado"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:132
msgid "``not_osre``: true if OSR is not empty (hasn't reached its threshold)"
msgstr ""
"``not_osre``: verdadero si el OSR no está vacío (no ha alcanzado su umbral)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:135
msgid "*label*: label to jump to if condition is true"
msgstr "*label*: etiqueta a la que saltar si la condición es verdadera"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:137
msgid "wait(polarity, src, index)"
msgstr "wait(polarity, src, index)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:138
msgid "Block, waiting for high/low on a pin or IRQ line."
msgstr "Se bloquea, esperando un nivel alto/bajo en un pin o una línea IRQ."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:140
msgid "*polarity*: 0 or 1, whether to wait for a low or high value"
msgstr "*polarity*: 0 o 1, indica si se espera un valor bajo o alto"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:141
msgid ""
"*src*: one of: ``gpio`` (absolute pin), ``pin`` (pin relative to "
"StateMachine's ``in_base`` argument), ``irq``"
msgstr ""
"*src*: uno de: ``gpio`` (pin absoluto), ``pin`` (pin relativo al argumento "
"``in_base`` de la StateMachine), ``irq``"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:143
msgid "*index*: 0-31, the index for *src*"
msgstr "*index*: 0-31, el índice para *src*"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:145
msgid "in_(src, bit_count)"
msgstr "in_(src, bit_count)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:146
msgid "Shift data in from *src* to ISR."
msgstr "Desplaza datos hacia dentro desde *src* al ISR."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:148
msgid "*src*: one of: ``pins``, ``x``, ``y``, ``null``, ``isr``, ``osr``"
msgstr "*src*: uno de: ``pins``, ``x``, ``y``, ``null``, ``isr``, ``osr``"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:149
msgid "*bit_count*: number of bits to shift in (1-32)"
msgstr "*bit_count*: número de bits a desplazar hacia dentro (1-32)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:151
msgid "out(dest, bit_count)"
msgstr "out(dest, bit_count)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:152
msgid "Shift data out from OSR to *dest*."
msgstr "Desplaza datos hacia fuera desde el OSR a *dest*."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:154
msgid ""
"*dest*: one of: ``pins``, ``x``, ``y``, ``pindirs``, ``pc``, ``isr``, "
"``exec``"
msgstr ""
"*dest*: uno de: ``pins``, ``x``, ``y``, ``pindirs``, ``pc``, ``isr``, "
"``exec``"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:156
msgid "*bit_count*: number of bits to shift out (1-32)"
msgstr "*bit_count*: número de bits a desplazar hacia fuera (1-32)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:158
msgid "push(...)"
msgstr "push(...)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:159
msgid ""
"Push ISR to the RX FIFO, then clear ISR to zero. This instruction takes the "
"following forms:"
msgstr ""
"Empuja el ISR a la FIFO de RX y luego pone el ISR a cero. Esta instrucción "
"admite las siguientes formas:"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:162
msgid "push()"
msgstr "push()"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:163
msgid "push(block)"
msgstr "push(block)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:164
msgid "push(noblock)"
msgstr "push(noblock)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:165
msgid "push(iffull)"
msgstr "push(iffull)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:166
msgid "push(iffull, block)"
msgstr "push(iffull, block)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:167
msgid "push(iffull, noblock)"
msgstr "push(iffull, noblock)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:169
msgid ""
"If ``block`` is used then the instruction stalls if the RX FIFO is full. The"
" default is to block.  If ``iffull`` is used then it only pushes if the "
"input shift count has reached its threshold."
msgstr ""
"Si se usa ``block``, la instrucción se detiene si la FIFO de RX está llena. "
"El comportamiento predeterminado es bloquear. Si se usa ``iffull``, solo se "
"empuja si el contador de desplazamiento de entrada ha alcanzado su umbral."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:173
msgid "pull(...)"
msgstr "pull(...)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:174
msgid ""
"Pull from the TX FIFO into OSR. This instruction takes the following forms:"
msgstr ""
"Extrae de la FIFO de TX hacia el OSR. Esta instrucción admite las siguientes"
" formas:"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:177
msgid "pull()"
msgstr "pull()"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:178
msgid "pull(block)"
msgstr "pull(block)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:179
msgid "pull(noblock)"
msgstr "pull(noblock)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:180
msgid "pull(ifempty)"
msgstr "pull(ifempty)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:181
msgid "pull(ifempty, block)"
msgstr "pull(ifempty, block)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:182
msgid "pull(ifempty, noblock)"
msgstr "pull(ifempty, noblock)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:184
msgid ""
"If ``block`` is used then the instruction stalls if the TX FIFO is empty. "
"The default is to block.  If ``ifempty`` is used then it only pulls if the "
"output shift count has reached its threshold."
msgstr ""
"Si se usa ``block``, la instrucción se detiene si la FIFO de TX está vacía. "
"El comportamiento predeterminado es bloquear. Si se usa ``ifempty``, solo se"
" extrae si el contador de desplazamiento de salida ha alcanzado su umbral."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:188
msgid "mov(dest, src)"
msgstr "mov(dest, src)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:189
msgid "Move into *dest* the value from *src*."
msgstr "Mueve a *dest* el valor de *src*."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:191
msgid ""
"*dest*: one of: ``pins``, ``x``, ``y``, ``exec``, ``pc``, ``isr``, ``osr``"
msgstr ""
"*dest*: uno de: ``pins``, ``x``, ``y``, ``exec``, ``pc``, ``isr``, ``osr``"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:192
msgid ""
"*src*: one of: ``pins``, ``x``, ``y``, ``null``, ``status``, ``isr``, "
"``osr``; this argument can be optionally modified by wrapping it in "
"``invert()`` or ``reverse()`` (but not both together)"
msgstr ""
"*src*: uno de: ``pins``, ``x``, ``y``, ``null``, ``status``, ``isr``, "
"``osr``; este argumento puede modificarse opcionalmente envolviéndolo en "
"``invert()`` o ``reverse()`` (pero no ambos a la vez)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:196
msgid "irq(...)"
msgstr "irq(...)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:197
msgid "Set or clear an IRQ flag. This instruction takes two forms:"
msgstr ""
"Establece o borra una bandera IRQ. Esta instrucción admite dos formas:"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:200
msgid "irq(index)"
msgstr "irq(index)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:201 ../../library/rp2.rst:205
msgid "*index*: 0-7, or ``rel(0)`` to ``rel(7)``"
msgstr "*index*: 0-7, o de ``rel(0)`` a ``rel(7)``"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:203
msgid "irq(mode, index)"
msgstr "irq(mode, index)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:204
msgid "*mode*: one of: ``block``, ``clear``"
msgstr "*mode*: uno de: ``block``, ``clear``"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:207
msgid ""
"If ``block`` is used then the instruction stalls until the flag is cleared "
"by another entity.  If ``clear`` is used then the flag is cleared instead of"
" being set.  Relative IRQ indices add the state machine ID to the IRQ index "
"with modulo-4 addition.  IRQs 0-3 are visible from to the processor, 4-7 are"
" internal to the state machines."
msgstr ""
"Si se usa ``block``, la instrucción se detiene hasta que otra entidad borre "
"la bandera. Si se usa ``clear``, la bandera se borra en lugar de "
"establecerse. Los índices IRQ relativos suman el ID de la máquina de estados"
" al índice IRQ con suma módulo 4. Las IRQ 0-3 son visibles para el "
"procesador, y las 4-7 son internas de las máquinas de estados."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:213
msgid "set(dest, data)"
msgstr "set(dest, data)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:214
msgid "Set *dest* with the value *data*."
msgstr "Establece *dest* con el valor *data*."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:216
msgid "*dest*: ``pins``, ``x``, ``y``, ``pindirs``"
msgstr "*dest*: ``pins``, ``x``, ``y``, ``pindirs``"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:217
msgid "*data*: value (0-31)"
msgstr "*data*: valor (0-31)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:219
msgid "nop()"
msgstr "nop()"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:220
msgid ""
"This is a pseudoinstruction that assembles to ``mov(y, y)`` and has no side "
"effect."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una pseudoinstrucción que se ensambla como ``mov(y, y)`` y no tiene "
"ningún efecto secundario."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:223
msgid ".side(value)"
msgstr ".side(value)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:224
msgid ""
"This is a modifier which can be applied to any instruction, and is used to "
"control side-set pin values."
msgstr ""
"Este es un modificador que puede aplicarse a cualquier instrucción y se usa "
"para controlar los valores de los pines side-set."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:227
msgid "*value*: the value (bits) to output on the side-set pins"
msgstr "*value*: el valor (bits) a emitir en los pines side-set"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:229
msgid ".delay(value)"
msgstr ".delay(value)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:230
msgid ""
"This is a modifier which can be applied to any instruction, and specifies "
"how many cycles to delay for after the instruction executes."
msgstr ""
"Este es un modificador que puede aplicarse a cualquier instrucción y "
"especifica cuántos ciclos retrasar tras la ejecución de la instrucción."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:233
msgid ""
"*value*: cycles to delay, 0-31 (maximum value reduced if side-set pins are "
"used)"
msgstr ""
"*value*: ciclos a retrasar, 0-31 (el valor máximo se reduce si se usan pines"
" side-set)"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:236
msgid "[value]"
msgstr "[value]"

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:237
msgid "This is a modifier and is equivalent to ``.delay(value)``."
msgstr "Este es un modificador y es equivalente a ``.delay(value)``."

#: ../../library/rp2.rst:241
msgid "Classes"
msgstr "Clases"
